# Data tables — everything tabular/binary in data/ stays local.
# The schema/config JSONs (category_taxonomy, global_filters, master_metadata*)
# are the deliberate exception and stay tracked.
data/*.csv
data/*.tsv
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls
# ...except the design workbook: category counts, the reviewed cat_4 folding
# behind category_taxonomy.json, per-category field coverage, and the pipeline
# spec extract_features.py was written from. Curated by hand, not generated.
!data/Item Features.xlsx
data/*.pkl
data/*.parquet
data/*.feather
data/*.npy
data/*.npz
data/*.h5
data/*.hdf5
data/*.db
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite3
data/*.zip
data/*.gz
# Pickle backups (df_features.pkl.bak-YYYYMMDD)
data/*.pkl.bak*

# Raw source dataset (~16 GB) — the schema/config JSONs in data/ stay tracked
data/meta_Home_and_Kitchen.json

# Generated tables anywhere in the repo, not just data/. The rules above are
# path-scoped, so a pickle or CSV written next to a notebook — e.g. a pair
# table saved into complementary_cats_pairs/ or ttn/ — would otherwise be
# committed. It is still a generated data table and still stays local.
*.pkl
*.csv

# IDE
.idea/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
